{"title":"2020 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Alternate_Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Alternate Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Scientific_Notation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Scientific Notation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Logarithms_Without_Words)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Logarithms Without Words)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(reworded_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (reworded Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_CRITICALLY_THINK)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO CRITICALLY THINK)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The decimal representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce6559c22b38f698ff7b67ddc88f2d4d89c4084.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{1}{20^{20}}\\]\" width=\"32\" height=\"37\" /> consists of a string of zeros after the decimal point, followed by a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and then several more digits. How many zeros are in that initial string of zeros after the decimal point?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61ac1a4b5062d6c547943a876e3c8c2161ae2278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\text{ 23} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)} \\text{ 24} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)} \\text{ 25} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)} \\text{ 26} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)} \\text{ 27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"387\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad8d5ac8a5d2aa9c9319a5d7a0f4bb219e791abe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{1}{20^{20}} = \\dfrac{1}{(10\\cdot2)^{20}}=\\dfrac{1}{10^{20}\\cdot2^{20}}\\]\" width=\"226\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Now we do some estimation. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/7/b27adc0a8e8a598d8bc4e701cc94411d2b28954f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{20} = 1024^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/f/f6f4fb515f1d3a096a15a3bdce0db5aab3c5503f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{20}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> is a little more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e46242b6ae49af1fbf9566e27e2565faf1969e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000^2=1,000,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />. Multiplying it with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/5/655d6f5e5e2e41425fcdb6f35573a19062a10b58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />, we get that the denominator is about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/40609675b302564c0bb98f78bb425f4acc8eb2a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\underbrace{00\\dots0}_{26 \\text{ zeros}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"67\" height=\"34\" />. Notice that when we divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> digit number as long as n is not a power of 10, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> zeros before the first nonzero digit. This means that when we divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> digit integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/40609675b302564c0bb98f78bb425f4acc8eb2a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\underbrace{00\\dots0}_{26 \\text{ zeros}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"67\" height=\"34\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/5/eb56cf14b3753a3b637d6f3c1488e61d7b39a611.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\text{26}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" /> zeros in the initial string after the decimal point. -PCChess\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a28e2d85f1a09e91bc2cf2367b6def0652e0f34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{20^{20}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"34\" height=\"37\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/5/b75a5af95e034fe65d2f78cda260e44847b1f892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5^{20}}{10^{40}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"34\" height=\"39\" />. Then, we know that when we write this in decimal form, there will be 40 digits after the decimal point. Therefore, we just have to find the number of digits in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79f3b5039d3b8e5fbe569dd2e7df0b176dc5f2d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${5^{20}}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/b/a1b1fca3a19735162ac72cdc1c11e36c6f86c947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log{5^{20}} = 20\\log{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" /> and memming <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dd439da34f8e148ca1cc7c510e18caee6ec9f8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log{5}\\approx0.69$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> (alternatively use the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/5/2c512a6ac67c90f3c61f10bc86868bf3343d90f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log{5} = 1 - \\log{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"126\" height=\"16\" />), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/528a66c6a5a21c4867d7ace01fb4b4780a91e16a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor{20\\log{5}}\\rfloor+1=\\lfloor{20\\cdot0.69}\\rfloor+1=13+1=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"355\" height=\"19\" /> digits. \n</p><p>Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/5/eb56cf14b3753a3b637d6f3c1488e61d7b39a611.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\text{26}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Brute_Force)\">Solution 3 (Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Just as in Solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1d1407aac4125d6c453a365eb173d96ebb48e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> we rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/a/78a95241cd431520b1d19d8b6afba089391af9ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{20^{20}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"34\" height=\"37\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/783e74ad1457329600b4bb422acd9ae97d272978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{5^{20}}{10^{40}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"39\" height=\"39\" /> We then calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5cc39c93c350a7c65e1b10bbd0b5e8385080b4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> entirely by hand, first doing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5e143ecedb9d2d57cee126269e0a91ed3135b9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^5 \\cdot 5^5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> then multiplying that product by itself, resulting in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e28d5e4d15ecdd4faf9c09bac5ce2721b1ea2f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$95,367,431,640,625.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"17\" /> Because this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> digits, after dividing this number by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> fourteen times, the decimal point is before the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6a1b9d5cec741422bfb37f91db47fd7514f5377.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> Dividing the number again by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> twenty-six more times allows a string of<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/5/eb56cf14b3753a3b637d6f3c1488e61d7b39a611.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\text{26}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" /> zeroes to be formed. -OreoChocolate\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Alternate_Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Alternate_Brute_Force)\">Solution 4 (Alternate Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Alternate Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Just as in Solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f885f96d2fb7e65f800de4ff71d7dcd0a5d2db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> we rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/a/78a95241cd431520b1d19d8b6afba089391af9ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{20^{20}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"34\" height=\"37\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/783e74ad1457329600b4bb422acd9ae97d272978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{5^{20}}{10^{40}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"39\" height=\"39\" /> We can then look at the number of digits in powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/32115eecc1fb065e5cee4ac42ceaaae727698d47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^1=5$\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab660081d421ba9ad93273259efac9a7e27639a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2=25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a3f26200911534c37a95b55a5baba4d3d4a113.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^3=125$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f18ab4678b134fb87a795ecc52ad7ef06650f456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^4=625$\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/b/e0bbe5f92fa7fec6faf4195278b19c2b79e51b39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^5=3125$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b301e4b5383022bc349347f78436ff13e11851d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^6=15625$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/4/8a4ec3454413d83257fa3cf401edf65f2ab4daca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^7=78125$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> and so on. We notice after a few iterations that every power of five with an exponent of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae77bfc5258833f636b36babcfad6633ad2bc0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\mod 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, the number of digits doesn't increase. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5cc39c93c350a7c65e1b10bbd0b5e8385080b4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> should have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/0/9604ee4128c8d5262299800c42e38528869f8e3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 - 6$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> digits since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers which are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae77bfc5258833f636b36babcfad6633ad2bc0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\mod 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> digits total. This means our expression can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be08c7a8838b778f2bb1f6081f0120ad90b8eb7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{k\\cdot10^{14}}{10^{40}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"39\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55a5922850cb36b035b7d64e193b6f70bf2b74f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[1,10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />. Canceling gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d081b05fb1a238e42b3f7790a360b51c294531e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{k}{10^{26}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"34\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> zeroes before the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> since the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> should start on where the one would be in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/6/d3653b61b4b8a398e72fa8e0b2c2d67db566ff65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />. ~aop2014\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Scientific_Notation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Scientific_Notation)\">Solution 5 (Scientific Notation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Scientific Notation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ac04941f0b2e63481160e5054fe3331f6b8f07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{20^{20}} = 9.5367432 \\cdot \\cdot \\cdot \\times 10^{-27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"228\" height=\"38\" />. We see that this has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/97521cb5ac5791d6248d8468c67de507a8e7209d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27-1=26$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> zeros after the decimal point before coming to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/a/0aac775f6ade638c1b7e3b74db0092f2a7a4bb76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} ~26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p><br />\nbut how would this be possible without the use of a calculator?\n</p><p>(Brute Force)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Logarithms_Without_Words.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Logarithms_Without_Words)\">Solution 6 (Logarithms Without Words)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Logarithms Without Words)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c01e4fcb5bdef3c90398371048fc69fd2b952d35.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}|\\lceil \\log \\dfrac{1}{20^{20}} \\rceil| &amp;= |\\lceil \\log 20^{-20} \\rceil| \\\\ &amp;= |\\lceil -20 \\log(20) \\rceil| \\\\ &amp;= |\\lceil -20(\\log 10 + \\log 2) \\rceil| \\\\ &amp;= |\\lceil -20(1 + 0.301) \\rceil| \\\\ &amp;= |\\lceil -26.02 \\rceil| \\\\ &amp;= |-26| \\\\ &amp;= \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\text{26}} \\end{align*}\" width=\"284\" height=\"197\" />\n</p><p>~phoenixfire\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Algebra)\">Solution 7 (Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> as the number of consecutive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s after the decimal point in the decimal representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfa6d6c4e8291cf9be4ad30d5445f501ff1cc39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{20^{20}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"43\" height=\"38\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cac1f6bc2cdbf5cc739001f384cb10241bed45fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{10^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> zeroes followed by a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when expressed as a decimal, and is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfa6d6c4e8291cf9be4ad30d5445f501ff1cc39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{20^{20}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"43\" height=\"38\" /> So, we have that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/0/c206ac7aef925ce00702bb15702b5fc134518c61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{10^n} &gt; \\frac{1}{20^{20}}.\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"37\" />\nTaking the reciprocal and switching signs grants\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8160b35083cfb3c2d6c337569c4b7e72fddf1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[20^{20}&gt;10^n.\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />\nWe can express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/b/38b10853d4ecaf618fdfcd13f4c73fe4d206ff59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20^{20}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff0e17262ed9d88a5a54b24ff8898b7f169a97f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{20} \\cdot 1024^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" /> We know that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9dd766c4d1b0ab91eb02cc05a84f7b4a2c8561c0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}  (1000 + 24)^2 &amp;= 1024^2 \\\\ 1000000 + 48000 + 576 &amp;= 1048576. \\end{align*}\" width=\"270\" height=\"42\" />\nMultiplying this with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/5/655d6f5e5e2e41425fcdb6f35573a19062a10b58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> adds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> more zeroes at the end, which means the left side of our inequality has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> digits. Then, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> on the right side must have an exponent less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967d7c9949f3e5d7e32b8be4df29d248885bae3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d971ac716a3d524bfd2157a076a9396820f043.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&lt;27.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We are also given that the initial string of zeroes in the decimal representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a28e2d85f1a09e91bc2cf2367b6def0652e0f34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{20^{20}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"34\" height=\"37\" /> is followed by a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6a1b9d5cec741422bfb37f91db47fd7514f5377.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> If we consider just these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> digits after the decimal point, we can express it as the fraction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e599d5711eb7ac0ede7868a7c1ecd192357e707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{10^{n+1}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"38\" /> Since there are more digits after this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the decimal representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/087cedb98cc07017ba638ce0203fd41603a132e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{20^{20}},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"43\" height=\"38\" /> it is true that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/3/a63c786b43721c9b74bb72d0b2112fb5417e2d8f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{20^{20}} &gt; \\frac{9}{10^{n+1}}.\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"37\" />\nRinse and repeat and we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5dfc05dd61a2564e8fb8f330403d53fd5f24e924.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[20^{20} &lt; \\frac{10^{n+1}}{9}.\\]\" width=\"107\" height=\"39\" />\nMultiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/5/c15ca289a74ebd8acd960e912a41290d83ef9324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{10^{20}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/7/467da3f09c1d8229315ccf30f2464c307caa1f47.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9 \\cdot 2^{20} &lt; 10^{n-19}.\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />\nWe previously found that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddf8a120f68fc9a16467b69eace2e1fdd74b6b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{20} = 1048576,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" /> which has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits. Multiplying this by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will keep the number of digits the same (make sure to see why). Thus, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d401b1290da861e93505665f4c2b136daae2151b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n-19&gt;6 \\qquad \\text{or} \\qquad n &gt; 25.\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0dd0d29413d8dc73fb48d0a15bd904eb2748467.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&lt;27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/a/43a457873f2e843e5bf3ee740cc76304cdc378a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;25,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/c/59c264ab7f3f231701c9b1fc9328c7665e672f35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n= \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\ 26}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"107\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~happyhari, mathbrek\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28reworded_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(reworded_Solution_1)\">Solution 8 (reworded Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (reworded Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We split <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a28e2d85f1a09e91bc2cf2367b6def0652e0f34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{20^{20}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"34\" height=\"37\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/e/b1e945d489657360f2fa0d213a3cd87f55db1c61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2^{20}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{10^{20}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" />. Memorizing(or just multiplying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96e8dedb32ce99214f8d25a98385072c8f2e778e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1024 \\cdot 1024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" />) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/1/7016a1148a41e81b067f87528226c59f77b01d69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{20} = 1048576$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"17\" />, we know that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa80633a81fa52aa395c1d2112327cecece82a11.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{1000000} &lt; \\frac{1}{2^{20}} = \\frac{1}{1048576}.\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Taking notice of the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/743519787c835be88fbcc04b7a8c5f90f7aabf2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{1000000} = 10^{-6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" /> and has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> zeroes following the decimal point, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/757c7e3245b005ae60b6b7280cecfe1c1cd01085.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{1048576}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" /> must be a bit smaller than that and therefore have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of them. So, multiplying that up with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/3916948903a6a17272fae6ad2f00b7d2e4c37fcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{10^{20}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" /> would give another <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> zeroes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2ca7a05ad370f0a40a43abf36b5267cb52c4a032.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{-20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, and therefore there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/1/0f1a878d04c3e79a8c24f5feb4790cbd81013823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 + 6 = \\boxed{26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" /> zeroes following the decimal point in the original fraction.\n</p><p>by DearPrince\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/t6yjfKXpwDs\">https://youtu.be/t6yjfKXpwDs</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_CRITICALLY_THINK.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_CRITICALLY_THINK)\">Video Solution (HOW TO CRITICALLY THINK)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO CRITICALLY THINK)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/qnznImCDSW4\">https://youtu.be/qnznImCDSW4</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B\" title=\"2020 AMC 10B\">2020 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2020 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2020 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=